[Music]  it didn't look a lot like christmas this  year in bethlehem  celebrations were restricted to the bare  minimum  as coveted 19 cases surge  [Music]  only few worshipers were allowed to  attend the midnight mass in the church  of the nativity  the pandemic with with its burden of  suffering and death  asks us to imagine a different world  made up of new solidarity and fraternal  relationships  where possessing is replaced by  giving and the wealth of  a few becomes a benefit for everyone  the palestinian president and many  foreign diplomats  didn't join the christmas service  the day started with a low-key reception  of the latin patriarch of jerusalem  a procession to welcome him usually  attracts thousands  this year he gave his blessings from a  distance  you can feel the town's sadness this is  not how christmas looks  it's also the first time that we didn't  attend the christmas tree lightning  ceremony  palestine's first cases of copper 19  were reported in bethlehem in march  tourism dried up in a country that  heavily depends on it  the tourism ministry says that losses  this year  are estimated at one and a half billion  dollars  rafa chomeli makes a living out of  tourism he arranges community-based tour  guides  and says 2019 was a very good season  now he expects his business to pick up  in october  of next year we had fully booked maybe a  year in advance  it was the first time maybe we had this  since the birth of jesus you know  so it was amazing we were expecting an  amazing year and  things have changed but it's going to be  back  i pray  almost all christmas related festivities  were called off  instead pre-recorded christmas carols  were broadcasted online  the palestinian authority says it tried  to limit gatherings as much as possible  to combat the spread of the coronavirus  this year  there are fewer christmas lights and  decorations than usual  but some here tell us that the message  of christmas is  all about hope and they're praying that  next year  will be better ibrahim  the occupied west bank

